<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 1.36 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 1.36 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland said it fixed the zloty at 3.2705 to the dollar, up from 3.2955 on Friday and at 1.8715 to the mark, up from 1.8800.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.36 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Friday's 0.72 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
